      correctIndex: 1,
      explanation: `<div style="--mx-navy:#01506e; --mx-blue:#207bb5; --mx-lightblue:#0099d4; --mx-yellow:#e9dc12; --mx-grey:#4B556A; --mx-rule:#dde4ea; --mx-tint:#f2f7fa; --mx-body:#232a33; color:var(--mx-body); line-height:1.6"><div style="background:var(--mx-tint); border-left:4px solid var(--mx-yellow); padding:13px 18px; margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">B. $356,000 is correct.</strong> Only three of the four items move cash: $375,000 out for the bonds, $31,000 out for dividends, and $50,000 in from the treasury stock sale.</div><h3 style="color:var(--mx-navy); font-size:17px; margin:0 0 8px">The rule</h3><p style="margin:0 0 12px">The financing section reports the <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">actual cash exchanged</strong> with lenders and owners (<strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">ASC 230</strong>), never the carrying amount of whatever changed hands. Financing covers debt principal, equity issues and repurchases, and dividends paid; interest paid stays in operating. Early retirement of debt is an outflow equal to the <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">full cash paid</strong>, $375,000. The $5,000 paid above the $370,000 carrying amount is a <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">loss on the income statement</strong>, not a separate line in any cash flow section.</p><p style="margin:0 0 18px">Dividends are a financing outflow in the period the <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">cash leaves</strong>, so the Year 1 declaration date does not matter. The treasury stock sale brings in the <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">full $50,000 of proceeds</strong>; the $7,000 above cost is credited to paid-in capital and is never stripped out of the cash line. Converting preferred stock into common shares is <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">noncash</strong>: one equity account is reclassified into another, so it belongs in the <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">supplemental schedule</strong> of noncash financing activities and adds nothing to the total.</p><h3 style="color:var(--mx-navy); font-size:17px; margin:0 0 8px">The math</h3><div style="background:var(--mx-tint); border-left:4px solid var(--mx-blue); padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:18px"><table style="border:0; border-collapse:collapse; width:100%"><tbody><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Payment to retire bonds payable</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$(375,000)</td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Dividend paid to preferred shareholders</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$(31,000)</td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Proceeds from sale of treasury stock</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$50,000</td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Conversion of preferred into common, noncash</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$0</td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Net cash used in financing activities</strong></td><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">$(356,000)</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 style="color:var(--mx-navy); font-size:17px; margin:0 0 8px">The entries</h3><div style="background:var(--mx-tint); border-left:4px solid var(--mx-blue); padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:18px"><table style="border:0; border-collapse:collapse; width:100%"><tbody><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Account</strong></td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Debit</strong></td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Credit</strong></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Bonds payable</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">370,000</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Loss on early retirement of bonds</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">5,000</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px 11px 40px">Cash</td><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">375,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="background:var(--mx-tint); border-left:4px solid var(--mx-blue); padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:18px"><table style="border:0; border-collapse:collapse; width:100%"><tbody><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Account</strong></td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Debit</strong></td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Credit</strong></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Cash</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">50,000</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px 11px 40px">Treasury stock</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">43,000</td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px 11px 40px">Additional paid-in capital</td><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">7,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="margin:0">Both entries hit cash for the <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">gross amount</strong>, and that gross amount is what the financing section reports. Watch for the trap of netting the $50,000 against the $43,000 cost or reporting only the $370,000 carrying amount: both understate the true cash movement.</p></div>`,
